--TEST--
`$uri->with` carries an omitted component over and removes one a written `null` names, and `""` is a value rather than a removal — rule:core-api/omission-is-not-a-written-null, rule:core-api/a-written-null-removes, rule:core-classes/uri-removable-components
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Uri::with
// The two ways of not giving a component a value are two different requests.
// `{}` leaves every one of the six alone; `{fragment: null}` clears exactly the
// one it names and carries the other five over.
var $u = Core\Uri::parse("https://example.com:8443/a?x=1#top");
echo $u->with({})->toString(), "\n";
echo $u->with({fragment: null})->toString(), "\n";
echo $u->with({port: null, query: null})->toString(), "\n";

// Three components are removable and each reader answers `null` afterwards —
// `port`, `query` and `fragment`, which are the three whose absence a URI can
// spell at all.
var $bare = $u->with({port: null, query: null, fragment: null});
echo $bare->toString(), "\n";
echo $bare->port() == null, "|", $bare->query() == null, "|", $bare->fragment() == null, "\n";

// `""` is not a second removal spelling: an empty query is a value, which is
// what `?` written with nothing after it produces, and `query()` tells it from
// an absent one. The two `with` calls therefore answer two different URIs.
var $empty = $u->with({query: ""});
var $gone = $u->with({query: null});
echo $empty->toString(), "|", $empty->query() == null, "\n";
echo $gone->toString(), "|", $gone->query() == null, "\n";

// The same key that removes with `null` replaces with a value, so nothing about
// replacement moved to make room for this.
echo $u->with({port: 443, query: "y=2", fragment: "b"})->toString(), "\n";

// A fresh `Uri` every time: the receiver none of the above mentioned twice is
// still the URI it was parsed from.
echo $u->toString(), "\n";
--EXPECT--
https://example.com:8443/a?x=1#top
https://example.com:8443/a?x=1
https://example.com/a#top
https://example.com/a
1|1|1
https://example.com:8443/a?#top|
https://example.com:8443/a#top|1
https://example.com:443/a?y=2#b
https://example.com:8443/a?x=1#top
